WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.076 --> 00:00:01.089
- Today we're going to be talking

00:00:01.089 --> 00:00:03.249
about why law school is hard

00:00:03.249 --> 00:00:05.916
and how to make it easy and fun.

00:00:06.884 --> 00:00:09.955
Believe it or not, it can be fun.

00:00:09.955 --> 00:00:12.538
(mellow music)

00:00:14.624 --> 00:00:15.961
I remember in high school everyone said

00:00:15.961 --> 00:00:19.365
college was going to be twice
the work of high school.

00:00:19.365 --> 00:00:22.181
And when I got there, I found
that it wasn't so much harder

00:00:22.181 --> 00:00:24.357
than it was just different.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.354
Law school is the same way.

00:00:26.354 --> 00:00:29.001
It is very different from college.

00:00:29.001 --> 00:00:30.584
And while most people think it's harder,

00:00:30.584 --> 00:00:33.430
a lot of that is just a
self-fulfilling prophecy.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:37.142
It's more accurate to say
law school is different.

00:00:37.142 --> 00:00:39.681
Now everyone would, of course,
agree that in law school,

00:00:39.681 --> 00:00:41.461
you'll read more.

00:00:41.461 --> 00:00:43.270
The reading is challenging,

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:46.523
the subjects are unlike
anything you've seen before.

00:00:46.523 --> 00:00:48.531
And you won't really
have a frame of reference

00:00:48.531 --> 00:00:49.807
for those subjects.

00:00:49.807 --> 00:00:51.478
It's incredibly stressful and

00:00:51.478 --> 00:00:55.300
oh yeah, your entire
professional career as a lawyer

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.529
rests on getting good grades.

00:00:57.529 --> 00:00:58.757
So there's that.

00:00:58.757 --> 00:01:01.242
But most would say that
law school is hard,

00:01:01.242 --> 00:01:04.197
I think mainly because
of the lack of feedback.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:07.429
The lack of feedback makes people insane.

00:01:07.429 --> 00:01:09.069
They study constantly.

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:11.333
But because there is so little feedback,

00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:13.880
they don't know if they're
doing the right thing.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:18.425
You work for an entire semester
studying complex systems

00:01:18.425 --> 00:01:22.592
of law and it all comes
down to a single final exam.

00:01:23.499 --> 00:01:24.994
And here's the real issue.

00:01:24.994 --> 00:01:27.765
The final exam is a test that is nothing

00:01:27.765 --> 00:01:29.422
like anything in undergrad.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.885
Hell, it's nothing like the LSAT.

00:01:31.885 --> 00:01:35.620
As a result, many people
study the wrong things.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.064
And what's worse than that,
they study the wrong things

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:40.091
for a long time.

00:01:40.091 --> 00:01:42.924
They spend hundreds of
hours studying things

00:01:42.924 --> 00:01:45.201
that won't help them on the final.

00:01:45.201 --> 00:01:46.356
When you get to law school,

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:49.528
you have to think about the
end game, the end result.

00:01:49.528 --> 00:01:52.283
And then work backwards from there.

00:01:52.283 --> 00:01:54.472
We have a ton of videos on
how to succeed in law school,

00:01:54.472 --> 00:01:56.150
we'll put them in the links down below.

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:58.449
But suffice to say, there are lots of ways

00:01:58.449 --> 00:02:01.113
to create feedback during
the regular semester,

00:02:01.113 --> 00:02:04.853
and to figure out what's going
on before you take the test.

00:02:04.853 --> 00:02:07.700
Most importantly, you can
improve your law school

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.769
test-taking skills before
you get to the final.

00:02:10.769 --> 00:02:14.220
This is probably the single
biggest missed opportunity

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:17.171
in all of law school,
not learning how to write

00:02:17.171 --> 00:02:19.037
law school essays.

00:02:19.037 --> 00:02:20.620
It's just like the LSAT.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:23.719
You'll still have to study,
but you'll have to learn

00:02:23.719 --> 00:02:27.031
the strategies and improve
your score over time,

00:02:27.031 --> 00:02:29.567
and you do that by practicing.

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:31.620
But most people don't do that.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:32.680
Why?

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:36.270
Because if they did, they
might confirm their worst fear

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:39.317
that they are no longer
at the top of their class.

00:02:39.317 --> 00:02:41.984
But it's coming anyway,
whether they avoid it or not.

00:02:41.984 --> 00:02:45.065
And by avoiding the necessary practice,

00:02:45.065 --> 00:02:47.785
it again becomes a
self-fulfilling prophecy.

00:02:47.785 --> 00:02:50.154
One of the biggest problems in law school

00:02:50.154 --> 00:02:53.071
is that it's a game that
nobody tells you the rules.

00:02:53.071 --> 00:02:54.310
And think of it like this.

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:55.771
If you wanted to play chess,

00:02:55.771 --> 00:02:57.735
but your partner refused to explain

00:02:57.735 --> 00:03:00.517
how the pieces moved,
you'd be in big trouble.

00:03:00.517 --> 00:03:02.212
And it's the same with law school.

00:03:02.212 --> 00:03:04.310
But once you know how the pieces move,

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.551
you can learn strategies
that will tell you

00:03:06.551 --> 00:03:10.294
how to move those pieces,
why you're doing it.

00:03:10.294 --> 00:03:12.253
And when you know what you're doing,

00:03:12.253 --> 00:03:14.089
you can start crushing your opponents.

00:03:14.089 --> 00:03:16.108
And it's the same in law school.

00:03:16.108 --> 00:03:18.805
Once you learn how to take
a law school essay exam,

00:03:18.805 --> 00:03:21.061
you can then start crushing those, too.

00:03:21.061 --> 00:03:22.907
Law school takes hard work,

00:03:22.907 --> 00:03:24.496
and there's no getting around that.

00:03:24.496 --> 00:03:27.197
But most people work
harder than they need to,

00:03:27.197 --> 00:03:29.529
and they make it harder on themselves.

00:03:29.529 --> 00:03:32.319
Trust me, once you start
taking practice exams,

00:03:32.319 --> 00:03:35.353
you'll understand how the law works.

00:03:35.353 --> 00:03:37.157
You'll understand how to apply it.

00:03:37.157 --> 00:03:40.278
And that will make your
studying so much easier.

00:03:40.278 --> 00:03:41.932
Don't be one of those students

00:03:41.932 --> 00:03:45.821
who works too hard for too
long on the wrong things.

00:03:45.821 --> 00:03:48.050
Learn the strategies, get an edge,

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:50.680
and like anything, when
you get good at something,

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:52.296
you start having fun.

00:03:52.296 --> 00:03:54.459
Believe me, when you
get A's in law school,

00:03:54.459 --> 00:03:57.209
you'll start having a lot of fun.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:00.218
Oh, and by the way, if you
wanna get better grades

00:04:00.218 --> 00:04:02.377
